    as "single-threaded test" — false; `cargo test` runs this module's tests
    concurrently with sibling tests that call `Command::spawn`. Verified
    against the installed std source (library/std/src/sys/env/unix.rs,
    library/std/src/sys/process/env.rs) that the actual safety property holds
    for a different reason: `Command::spawn`'s environment capture goes
    through `env::vars_os()`, which takes std's process-wide `ENV_LOCK.read()`
    exactly like `set_var`/`remove_var` take `ENV_LOCK.write()` — reads and
    writes are already mutually exclusive regardless of thread. Fixed the
    comment to state that, not the false single-threaded claim.
